  "result": {
    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Interactive Features\ndescription: A consolidated Quarto check for Observable JS and browser-only Jupyter widgets.\naliases:\n  - Browser Interactivity\ntags:\n  - examples/computation\n  - examples/interactive\npublish: true\nformat: html\nexecute:\n  freeze: true\n  cache: true\n---\n\nThis temporary page checks client-side components that remain interactive after Quarto output is\nplaced inside the Quartz page frame. See [[Computational Features]] for Python tables and figures,\nand [[Markdown Features]] for the plain Markdown boundary.\n\n## Observable JS\n\nPython serialises data into the page with `ojs_define`. Observable filters and redraws it reactively\nin the browser.\n\n::: {#cell-interactive-data .cell execution_count=1}\n\n::: {#interactive-data .cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"ojs-define\">{\"contents\": [{\"name\": \"series\", \"value\": [{\"n\": 10, \"error\": 0.25}, {\"n\": 20, \"error\": 0.16}, {\"n\": 50, \"error\": 0.09}, {\"n\": 100, \"error\": 0.06}, {\"n\": 200, \"error\": 0.04}, {\"n\": 500, \"error\": 0.025}, {\"n\": 1000, \"error\": 0.018}]}]}</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n```{ojs}\n//| label: ojs-input\nviewof cutoff = Inputs.range([10, 1000], { value: 1000, step: 10, label: \"max samples\" })\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| label: ojs-derived\nfiltered = series.filter((row) => row.n <= cutoff)\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| label: ojs-readout\nmd`Showing **${filtered.length}** of **${series.length}** points, up to n = **${cutoff}**.`\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| label: ojs-palette\n//| echo: false\nseriesColor = (n) => getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue(`--qmd-chart-series-${n}`).trim()\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| label: ojs-plot\nPlot.plot({\n  marks: [\n    Plot.line(filtered, { x: \"n\", y: \"error\", stroke: seriesColor(1) }),\n    Plot.dot(filtered, { x: \"n\", y: \"error\", fill: seriesColor(1) })\n  ],\n  x: { type: \"log\", label: \"samples\" },\n  y: { type: \"log\", label: \"absolute error\" },\n  height: 300\n})\n```\n\n```{ojs}\n//| label: ojs-table\nInputs.table(filtered)\n```\n\n## Browser-only Jupyter widgets\n\nPublished widgets have no Python kernel behind them. `jslink` keeps this slider, progress bar, and\nreadout connected entirely in the browser.\n\n::: {#cell-linked-widgets .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport ipywidgets as widgets\n\nslider = widgets.IntSlider(\n    value=40, min=0, max=100, step=1, description=\"samples:\", continuous_update=True\n)\nprogress = widgets.IntProgress(value=40, min=0, max=100, description=\"coverage:\")\nreadout = widgets.IntText(value=40, description=\"value:\")\n\nwidgets.jslink((slider, \"value\"), (progress, \"value\"))\nwidgets.jslink((slider, \"value\"), (readout, \"value\"))\nwidgets.VBox([slider, progress, readout])\n```\n\n::: {#linked-widgets .cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">\n{\"model_id\":\"347c6c3b5aa54dafad82d2ea047aef09\",\"version_major\":2,\"version_minor\":0,\"quarto_mimetype\":\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\"}\n</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nTabs exercise widget layout handling:\n\n::: {#cell-tabbed-widgets .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntabs = widgets.Tab(\n    children=[\n        widgets.HTML(\"<p>Independent samples converge at a predictable rate.</p>\"),\n        widgets.HTML(\"<p>Correlated draws reduce the effective sample size.</p>\"),\n    ]\n)\ntabs.set_title(0, \"Independent\")\ntabs.set_title(1, \"Correlated\")\ntabs\n```\n\n::: {#tabbed-widgets .cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">\n{\"model_id\":\"2350712313d84163b459e2a515e7a113\",\"version_major\":2,\"version_minor\":0,\"quarto_mimetype\":\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\"}\n</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nFinally, `ipyleaflet` checks loading a third-party widget bundle:\n\n::: {#cell-leaflet-map .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfrom ipyleaflet import Map, Marker\n\nsite_map = Map(center=(43.6532, -79.3832), zoom=9)\nsite_map.add(Marker(location=(43.6532, -79.3832)))\nsite_map\n```\n\n::: {#leaflet-map .cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<script type=\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\">\n{\"model_id\":\"5eb54888c3e74222a48fdb14fd7fcfba\",\"version_major\":2,\"version_minor\":0,\"quarto_mimetype\":\"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json\"}\n</script>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nReturn to [[Publishing Examples]].\n\n",
